  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "R1 establishes that an MTP can achieve near-DFT fidelity in a closely related BCC refractory multicomponent alloy, while R2 shows that SRO supplies a meaningful energetic stabilization in essentially the same alloy family. R12 and R15 additionally indicate that finite-temperature electronic or Fermi-level DOS effects can alter alloy free energies, and R20 confirms the relevance of SRO-resolved atomistic states in another BCC refractory HEA. These records point toward combining a high-fidelity machine-learned potential with electronic and SRO free-energy corrections, but none describes liquid-phase MTP training, replacing EAM in melting calculations, or using the small MTP–DFT energy variance for FEP instead of TI. Thus the specific FEP-based acceleration would still require a substantial new idea."
